          title: Gaia Dynamic Registry (objects + lexicon)
          text: |-
            GaiaRegistryExt tracks dynamic gaia/canvas/* keys (rooms/*/objects/*/count+seed, lexicon/*/count+seed) that a static Select CHOP cannot represent - keys appear/disappear at runtime. Per-key alpha ramps in on appearance and decays out on disappearance (never snaps). seed_reduced = raw_seed % 16777216 is a deterministic precision-safe reduction for GLSL float32, NOT a re-hash - the FNV-1a identity from Gaia is preserved. Script CHOPs adapt registry state to channels; CHOP-to-TOP textures (channel=row, sample=column, matching zones_geo's established precedent) make it consumable by a future GLSL compute shader.

            Also tracks gaia/people/{name}/* (affinity/confidence/present) the same dynamic way. Unlike objects/lexicon, Gaia provides no seed for people, so each name's color comes from a LOCAL string hash (_nameHue) computed once and cached - not a rehash of any Gaia value, since there is nothing to rehash here. scriptchop_affinity exposes a single aggregate (r,g,b,intensity): a weighted-average identity color across everyone currently present (weight = presence-alpha times confidence, so an uncertain recognition contributes less), with intensity = weighted-average affinity - a stranger barely tints the scene, someone Gaia has a real bond with glows in proportion to that bond. Feeds the affinity_wash chain at the Visuals level via the same select-CHOP cross-COMP bridge used throughout this project.
