      - name: annotate1
        type: annotateCOMP
        sequences:
          ext:
          - object: op.TDAnnotate.mod.AnnotateExt.AnnotateExt(me)
            promote: true
        custom_pars:
          Text:
            $t: text
            Titletext: Gaia OSC Data Prep
            Bodytext: |-
              Selects and smooths soul/zone/metrics channels from oscin1 (710+ chans), bakes the 22-zone light state into a texture for GPU sampling. Also selects/lags YOLO presence counts (select_people/lag_people/null_people) and dynamically lists detected people/objects (script_detections) for the visual pipeline.

              MediaPipe (select_mediapipe/lag_mediapipe/null_mediapipe): flat per-room channels gaia/rooms/{salotto,ingresso}/mediapipe/{smile_score,mouth_open,eyes_open} - only these two rooms report today. soul_geo/glsl_soulfx's uSmile/uEyesOpen and noise1's amp0 read directly off these per-room channels (max for smile/mouth, min for eyes_open, computed inline in the expression) rather than through a dedicated aggregation script. This does not rescan dynamically if Gaia adds more mediapipe-covered rooms or moves to the newer people/{n}/ breakdown - a proper per-person, dynamic Script CHOP aggregator is the improvement path if that becomes necessary.

              NOTE: this data lives only on the legacy gaia/rooms/* path, not yet under gaia/canvas/* - if Gaia migrates it there this will need porting to data_canvas.
          Settings:
            $t: settings_2
            Mode: annotate
            Backcolorr:
            - '=me.color[0] # node color [r]'
            - =me.color[1]
            - '=me.color[2] '
          OP Viewer:
            $t: op_viewer
            Opvieweroversize: natural
          About:
            $t: about
        position: [-800, -1225]
        size: [438, 370]
        color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
        palette_clone: true
      - name: annotate2
        type: annotateCOMP
        sequences:
          ext:
          - object: op.TDAnnotate.mod.AnnotateExt.AnnotateExt(me)
            promote: true
        custom_pars:
          Text:
            $t: text
            Titletext: Soul + Zones Visual Pipeline
            Bodytext: |-
              POP/GLSL point-sprite scene: organic soul_geo core (stress/calm/energy/curiosity/social/lifeIndex driven) + zones_geo light ring (22 rooms), rendered and bloom-composited to out_null. Extended with YOLO/vision presence: additive per-room zone boost (salotto/ingresso/corridoio), subtle soul reactivity to total people count, and a bottom-left text overlay (names/objects) composited via over_detections before out_null. MediaPipe facial data also drives soul_geo: uSmile/uEyesOpen tint+dim the core color, mouth_open adds turbulence force to noise1's amplitude.

              Mood Wash: const_moodcolor -> level_moodwash -> moodwash_out inserts an ambient soul/mood_rgb color wash between render1 and level_bloom/composite_out, additive so it reads even in pure black. Controlled from moodwash_ctrl (Washamount/Washmode/Washlagtime), which also drives data_canvas/lag_mood_rgb's smoothing so the wash eases rather than snaps. soul_geo's pointsprite_soul material color is neutral white - glsl_soulfx_compute's Color[id] is the sole color source for the core, so the material never double-applies a tint.

              Events: event_watcher wildcard-scans gaia/canvas/event/level_up|dream_new and event_ctrl's Simlevelup/Simdreamnew manual toggles, detecting changes via a prev-vs-current comparison held in module-level state (not scriptOp.store, which caused a self-triggering cook loop when tried on the same op). Level-up: envelope_levelup (fast-rise/slow-decay Lag CHOP) feeds level_moodwash's opacity as an additive burst (Washamount + Burstamount*envelope), never a persistent state change. Dream: on a rising edge, event_watcher directly pulses timer_dream's Initialize+Start (the Timer CHOP's 2nd-input auto-trigger does not reliably restart once already "done", so direct pulsing is used instead), which runs dream_segments (fade-in/hold/fade-out, seconds). dream_visibility computes a 0-1 curve from timer_fraction/running/done, driving level_dream_render's opacity, composited via crossfade_dream (operand=over: dream must be input1/on top, base input2) onto an opaque dark dream_render1 backdrop (bgcolor alpha=1, not TOP's default 0) before out_null. dream_geo is seeded from registry/GetLexiconSlots (not a second registry) and uses the same primitivePOP method=set+keep=True fix as the other point-sprite geos.

              PLACEHOLDER: dream scene identity is seeded from lexicon words, not dream/mood + dream/words/* as originally intended - dream/mood is a string and TD's OSC In CHOP is float-only, with no numeric proxy the way mood_rgb backs soul/mood. Revisit once Gaia exposes a numeric dream/mood proxy or a second string-capable OSC port.

              Lexicon Sediment: glsl_sediment_deposit (glslTOP, 640x360 - matches the main scene's 16:9 aspect, avoiding stretch) reads registry/chopto_lexicon through an Out TOP (registry/out_lexicon), since a plain TOP wire cannot cross a COMP boundary and TOPs have no by-name reference parameter the way Select CHOP does for CHOPs. Deposits a tiny (0.0015-coefficient) seed-positioned mark per lexicon word every frame into feedback_sediment (bounded feedback loop, built bypassed first, reset=0 only after verifying passthrough) via level_sediment_decay (brightness1=Sedimentdecay, default 0.995, strictly <1) + comp_sediment_add. The deposit coefficient must stay tiny relative to (1-decay): the loop's steady-state value is deposit/(1-decay), and since every persistent word re-deposits every frame, too high a ratio saturates to solid white within seconds. Composited as a background substrate (over_sediment, render1 painted OVER the ink, render1's own background alpha=0/transparent so the ink shows through the void) before the mood wash, so recurring words fade in as a slow-building texture rather than a foreground flash. sediment_ctrl hosts Sedimentdecay/Sedimentamount/Sedimentreset (pulse, relayed to feedback_sediment's resetpulse via sediment_reset_relay, a Parameter Execute DAT, since pulse parameters can't be bound by expression).

              Lesson: Pixel Format left at "Use Input" on a chain rooted in a single-channel CHOP-to-TOP (registry/chopto_lexicon is genuinely mono, built with dataformat=r for texelFetch(...).r lookups) silently carries that mono-ness through every "useinput" node downstream - including the final composite (over_sediment), which then collapses the WHOLE FRAME's hue, not just the ink, since compositing duplicates R into G/B. All six sediment-chain TOPs (glsl_sediment_deposit, comp_sediment_add, feedback_sediment, level_sediment_decay, level_sediment_out, over_sediment) are set explicitly to "8-bit fixed (RGBA)" for this reason - never leave "useinput" downstream of a deliberately single-channel source.

              Affinity Wash: select_affinity bridges registry/scriptchop_affinity (the same cross-COMP CHOP-reference technique used throughout this project) -> lag_affinity (smoothing, Affinitylagtime) -> const_affinitycolor -> level_affinitywash (opacity = Affinityenable * Affinityamount * intensity), feeding moodwash_out as a third input (index 2, alongside over_sediment and level_moodwash) - moodwash_out is the shared ambient-wash hub for exactly this kind of addition. registry/GaiaRegistryExt tracks gaia/people/{name}/* the same dynamic way as objects/lexicon (alpha ramps on `present`, decays on absence); since Gaia provides no seed for people, each name's color comes from a locally-computed string hash, cached once per name. scriptchop_affinity's GetAffinityWash() aggregates everyone present into one (r,g,b,intensity): weight = presence-alpha * confidence, intensity = weighted-average affinity - a stranger barely tints the scene, a strong bond glows in proportion, multiple present people blend their identity colors together.

              Point-sprite additive blending (pointsprite_soul: blendop=add, srcblend=one, destblend=one) clips per-point color to white quickly once hundreds of points overlap. glsl_soulfx_compute's rim brightening is capped to 0.35+0.35*rim (peak channel stays ~0.665, safely under 1.0) so overlapping points still show internal gradient instead of flattening into a white shell; level_bloom (blacklevel 0.72, brightness2 1.2) and blur_bloom (size 12) are tuned tight so bloom only catches genuine highlights rather than smearing the remaining texture away.

              coolColor is (0.12, 0.95, 0.35) - green core, same peak channel magnitude as the tuning above so it still holds; warmColor (0.95, 0.28, 0.12, stress/smile accent) is unchanged, so high stress/smile still shifts the mix toward orange/red. Lesson: capturing intermediate TOPs one at a time in sequence (render1, then moodwash_out, then blur_bloom, then out_null) can return stale/inconsistently-cooked results relative to each other - always re-capture the actual final output fresh before judging whether a fix worked.

              Two webrenderTOPs (webrender1/webrender2) feed moodwash_out as additional additive inputs, compositing a sci-fi HUD/ring dashboard (level/archetype/vitals readout, glowing rings, particle starfield) over the soul core. soul_geo's scale is raised to 1.0 uniform (sx/sy/sz) so the core holds visual weight against that overlay instead of reading as a small dot in the middle.
          Settings:
            $t: settings_2
            Mode: annotate
            Backcolorr:
            - '=me.color[0] # node color [r]'
            - =me.color[1]
            - '=me.color[2] '
          OP Viewer:
            $t: op_viewer
            Opvieweroversize: natural
          About:
            $t: about
        position: [-70, -2805]
        size: [5690, 3275]
        color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
        palette_clone: true
      - name: annotate3
        type: annotateCOMP
        sequences:
          ext:
          - object: op.TDAnnotate.mod.AnnotateExt.AnnotateExt(me)
            promote: true
