            - '=me.color[2] '
          OP Viewer:
            $t: op_viewer
            Opvieweroversize: natural
          About:
            $t: about
        position: [-900, -2425]
        size: [580, 370]
        color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
        palette_clone: true
      - name: annotate5
        type: annotateCOMP
        sequences:
          ext:
          - object: op.TDAnnotate.mod.AnnotateExt.AnnotateExt(me)
            promote: true
        custom_pars:
          Text:
            $t: text
            Titletext: DMX Output (structure only, unarmed)
            Bodytext: |-
              select_lights_for_dmx (cross-boundary ref to data_canvas/null_lights_canvas) -> math_dmx_wash (gain=Lightscale, postoff=mood-wash contribution) -> merge_dmx -> limit_dmx (clamp 0-255) -> dmx_out1. Controlled from dmx_ctrl: Dmxenable (default OFF - safety switch, must be explicitly armed before any real hardware output), Washtodmxamount (mood wash fraction added to every fixture channel, additive so it reads even at power=0), Lightscale (raw-unit-to-255 multiplier, default 1.0 - all fixtures currently read 0 live, tune once real values are seen). dmx_patch table is a placeholder for the user to fill in fixture/universe/address once rig details are known. Protocol (Art-Net/sACN), universe, net/subnet left at defaults - structure only this pass.

              Virtual zone-color fixtures: script_zone_colors reads the 22 zones' final rendered Color attribute directly from zones_geo/glsl_zonelayout (the same on/off+brightness+motion+YOLO-presence-boost mix the visual actually shows per zone, not the raw Hue input state) as zone1_r..zone22_b (66 channels), scaled to 0-255 by math_zone_colors, merged with the existing house-mirroring channels in merge_dmx before the shared limit_dmx clamp - physical lights can be synced to the generative visual itself. Still gated by the same Dmxenable safety switch; these 66 channels have no routing table entries yet (structure only, unarmed - real fixture/universe/address assignment for a 22-fixture rig is the user's call).
          Settings:
            $t: settings_2
            Mode: annotate
            Backcolorr:
            - '=me.color[0] # node color [r]'
            - =me.color[1]
            - '=me.color[2] '
          OP Viewer:
            $t: op_viewer
            Opvieweroversize: natural
          About:
            $t: about
        position: [3450, 625]
        size: [2087, 783]
        color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
        palette_clone: true
      - name: annotate6
        type: annotateCOMP
        sequences:
          ext:
          - object: op.TDAnnotate.mod.AnnotateExt.AnnotateExt(me)
            promote: true
        custom_pars:
          Text:
            $t: text
            Titletext: Mocap Body Mirror
            Bodytext: |-
              Abstract "body mirror" driven by Gaia's gaia/mocap/ops-silvermini2/* feed (pose/hand/face landmarks, all three in use). mocap_bridge (MocapBridgeExt) is a DEFENSIVE adapter: the feed's channel addressing is unstable (pose/hand indices increment across tracking sessions instead of reusing fixed per-landmark slots; face is worse - mixed zero-padding widths like "01"/"010"/"0100"/"01000" sort out of numeric order alphabetically) - so identity is tracked by ACTIVITY (a channel's value changing between cooks, decaying like registry's alpha) rather than by literal channel name/index. A channel holding any real value stays visible at a STATIC_FLOOR alpha (0.3) even once it stops changing, since a manual/burst OSC test send has no continuous stream and would otherwise decay to invisible within ~1s.

              Bucketed active channels form up to 40 pose + 24+24 hand + 40 face points (128 total, grid_mocap sized 16x8). mocap_geo samples 4 CHOP-to-TOP textures (poseTex/handLTex/handRTex/faceTex) in a glslPOP compute shader (glsl_mocap), coloring each cluster with a distinct hue (pose 0.55 cyan, left hand 0.12 orange, right hand 0.92 pink, face 0.75 purple) mixed with mood color, fading via each point's activity-alpha.

              Lesson: pointsprite_mocap's Sizing Model is "Constant/Attenuate" with Attenuate Point Scale (attenpscale) raised to 0.6 (from a default of 0.0) and pointsize raised to 0.2 (from 0.025) - at attenpscale=0.0 the material completely ignores the shader's own PointScale attribute output and renders every point at the tiny constant size, which stayed invisible for a sparse, spread-out point cloud like this one (soul_geo's identical pointsize only looks visible because hundreds of densely-overlapping points accumulate brightness; a sparse body-tracing cloud has no such overlap). Attenuate Point Scale defaulting to 0.0 means a custom PointScale attribute from a compute shader has zero effect until raised - always verify a per-point size attribute is actually wired to something in the material, not just computed in the shader. A dedicated diagnostic render chain (mocap_preview_cam/mocap_preview_render/mocap_preview_out) stays in the network for isolating future render-visibility issues.

              Face construction: UpdateFace samples each of the 7 anatomical regions (lips/eye_left/eye_right/eyebrow_left/eyebrow_right/nose/oval, under gaia/mocap/ops-silvermini2/face/0/*) against a fixed per-region slot budget (_FACE_REGION_BUDGET: oval=10, lips=8, eye_left=6, eye_right=6, nose=6, eyebrow_left=2, eyebrow_right=2, summing to MAX_FACE_POINTS=40) so every region is always represented regardless of activity - pooling all regions globally and keeping the 40 most-active points let one busy region (e.g. lips while talking) crowd out the rest, producing a blob instead of a face. Within each region, points are sampled at evenly-spaced indices across that region's own contour (not top-K by activity), since MediaPipe contour indices are spatially ordered - this traces the region's actual outline shape instead of clustering on its busiest sub-area.
          Settings:
            $t: settings_2
            Mode: annotate
            Backcolorr:
            - '=me.color[0] # node color [r]'
            - =me.color[1]
            - '=me.color[2] '
          OP Viewer:
            $t: op_viewer
            Opvieweroversize: natural
          About:
            $t: about
        position: [512, 577]
        size: [1328, 818]
        color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
        palette_clone: true
      - name: annotate7
        type: annotateCOMP
        sequences:
          ext:
          - object: op.TDAnnotate.mod.AnnotateExt.AnnotateExt(me)
            promote: true
        custom_pars:
          Text:
            $t: text
            Titletext: Nursery Library (Canale 9)
            Bodytext: |-
              Pre-built, pre-tested components toggled by Bridge/gaia_nursery (MQTT gaia/nursery/activate|deactivate) -- see ARCHITECTURE.md §7 and GAIA_INTERFACE.md "Canale 9". Each component defaults to display=False/render=False (invisible, not cooking); the extension flips both flags and sets custom pars from the activation's params on activate, reverts on deactivate/TTL expiry. Whitelisted against nursery_components.json, never invented at runtime.

              person_sigil (trigger: person_recognized) -- wired into render1's Geometry list, appears in the main soul scene near recognition_geo. Custom pars: Hue, Shape (ring/spiral/cluster), Energy.
              dream_fragment (trigger: dream_new) -- wired into dream_render1's Geometry list (the separate dream-scene render, NOT the main render1), appears only when the dream crossfade is active. Custom pars: Hue, Shape (ring/spiral/cluster), Scale.

              Both share the same GLSL point-cluster technique (24 points, shape branches on an int uniform derived from the Shape menu) -- same pattern as recognition_geo/plantnotes_geo, kept deliberately small/cheap (confirmed negligible fps/GPU-mem impact via get_project_performance before/after).
          Settings:
            $t: settings_2
            Mode: annotate
            Backcolorr: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
          OP Viewer:
            $t: op_viewer
            Opvieweroversize: natural
          About:
            $t: about
        position: [1875, 600]
        size: [1289, 790]
        color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
        palette_clone: true
      - name: annotate8
        type: annotateCOMP
        sequences:
          ext:
          - object: op.TDAnnotate.mod.AnnotateExt.AnnotateExt(me)
            promote: true
        custom_pars:
          Text:
            $t: text
            Titletext: Plant Note Sparks (outer particle ring)
            Bodytext: |-
              16-slot ring buffer (GaiaRegistryExt._plantSlots, independent of the ambient plant_out wash's single-per-room aggregate) - each plant_note spawns one fading spark, packed via script_plantnotes_tex (80 chans, attribute-major: 16 r,16 g,16 b,16 bright,16 roomNorm) -> chopto_plantnotes (1x80 tex, rowscropped) -> glsl_plantnotes texelFetch, same pattern as zones_geo's zoneTex. Positioned in a ring (radius ~2.15-2.4, just outside the zone light ring at 2.0) with per-slot hash jitter on angle/radius/height so simultaneous notes in one room don't stack.

              Lessons from building this chain (all three silent - no errors, just wrong/no visual): (1) create_op leaves a new POP chain's Display/Render flags OFF by default (unlike TD's UI, which auto-activates the last-created op) - a geometryCOMP renders whichever child has the Render flag, so it must be set explicitly. (2) primitivePOP defaults to NOT converting the grid to point primitives - needs method=set, setprimtype=points, set=all, keep=True explicitly (same fix as dream_geo/inhabitants_geo), otherwise the underlying quad topology still renders as filled shapes. (3) An op whose only input is a static grid, with zero EXPRESSION-mode parameters, and whose live data arrives purely via a texture SAMPLER (not a wired input), cooks once and caches forever - TD has no reason to think it needs re-evaluation. Fixed by adding a uTime uniform (absTime.seconds, EXPRESSION mode, used for a faint per-point twinkle) purely to give it a reason to re-cook on demand; the real trigger is "has at least one EXPRESSION-mode par," not "references absTime specifically" (zones_geo/glsl_zonelayout already re-cooks correctly because it has EXPRESSION-mode vec pars, with no uTime at all).

              Camera note: radius >~2.5 at this COMP's depth (z=0, same as zones_geo) is outside the frustum (cam at z=6, fov=45, soul_geo at z=-2) - invisible off-frame if the ring is ever widened.
          Settings:
            $t: settings_2
            Mode: annotate
            Backcolorr:
            - '=me.color[0] # node color [r]'
            - =me.color[1]
            - '=me.color[2] '
          OP Viewer:
            $t: op_viewer
            Opvieweroversize: natural
          About:
            $t: about
        position: [3900, -2100]
        size: [1581, 500]
        color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
        palette_clone: true
