      annotations:
      - name: annotate1
        mode: annotate
        title: Gaia OSC Data Prep
        text: |-
          Selects and smooths soul/zone/metrics channels from oscin1 (710+ chans), bakes the 22-zone light state into a texture for GPU sampling. Also selects/lags YOLO presence counts (select_people/lag_people/null_people) and dynamically lists detected people/objects (script_detections) for the visual pipeline.

          MediaPipe (select_mediapipe/lag_mediapipe/null_mediapipe): flat per-room channels gaia/rooms/{salotto,ingresso}/mediapipe/{smile_score,mouth_open,eyes_open} - only these two rooms report today. soul_geo/glsl_soulfx's uSmile/uEyesOpen and noise1's amp0 read directly off these per-room channels (max for smile/mouth, min for eyes_open, computed inline in the expression) rather than through a dedicated aggregation script. This does not rescan dynamically if Gaia adds more mediapipe-covered rooms or moves to the newer people/{n}/ breakdown - a proper per-person, dynamic Script CHOP aggregator is the improvement path if that becomes necessary.

          NOTE: this data lives only on the legacy gaia/rooms/* path, not yet under gaia/canvas/* - if Gaia migrates it there this will need porting to data_canvas.
        position: [-800, -1225]
        size: [438, 370]
        color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
      - name: annotate2
        mode: annotate
        title: Soul + Zones Visual Pipeline
        text: |-
          POP/GLSL point-sprite scene: organic soul_geo core (stress/calm/energy/curiosity/social/lifeIndex driven) + zones_geo light ring (22 rooms), rendered and bloom-composited to out_null. Extended with YOLO/vision presence: additive per-room zone boost (salotto/ingresso/corridoio), subtle soul reactivity to total people count, and a bottom-left text overlay (names/objects) composited via over_detections before out_null. MediaPipe facial data also drives soul_geo: uSmile/uEyesOpen tint+dim the core color, mouth_open adds turbulence force to noise1's amplitude.

          Mood Wash: const_moodcolor -> level_moodwash -> moodwash_out inserts an ambient soul/mood_rgb color wash between render1 and level_bloom/composite_out, additive so it reads even in pure black. Controlled from moodwash_ctrl (Washamount/Washmode/Washlagtime), which also drives data_canvas/lag_mood_rgb's smoothing so the wash eases rather than snaps. soul_geo's pointsprite_soul material color is neutral white - glsl_soulfx_compute's Color[id] is the sole color source for the core, so the material never double-applies a tint.

          Events: event_watcher wildcard-scans gaia/canvas/event/level_up|dream_new and event_ctrl's Simlevelup/Simdreamnew manual toggles, detecting changes via a prev-vs-current comparison held in module-level state (not scriptOp.store, which caused a self-triggering cook loop when tried on the same op). Level-up: envelope_levelup (fast-rise/slow-decay Lag CHOP) feeds level_moodwash's opacity as an additive burst (Washamount + Burstamount*envelope), never a persistent state change. Dream: on a rising edge, event_watcher directly pulses timer_dream's Initialize+Start (the Timer CHOP's 2nd-input auto-trigger does not reliably restart once already "done", so direct pulsing is used instead), which runs dream_segments (fade-in/hold/fade-out, seconds). dream_visibility computes a 0-1 curve from timer_fraction/running/done, driving level_dream_render's opacity, composited via crossfade_dream (operand=over: dream must be input1/on top, base input2) onto an opaque dark dream_render1 backdrop (bgcolor alpha=1, not TOP's default 0) before out_null. dream_geo is seeded from registry/GetLexiconSlots (not a second registry) and uses the same primitivePOP method=set+keep=True fix as the other point-sprite geos.

          PLACEHOLDER: dream scene identity is seeded from lexicon words, not dream/mood + dream/words/* as originally intended - dream/mood is a string and TD's OSC In CHOP is float-only, with no numeric proxy the way mood_rgb backs soul/mood. Revisit once Gaia exposes a numeric dream/mood proxy or a second string-capable OSC port.

          Lexicon Sediment: glsl_sediment_deposit (glslTOP, 640x360 - matches the main scene's 16:9 aspect, avoiding stretch) reads registry/chopto_lexicon through an Out TOP (registry/out_lexicon), since a plain TOP wire cannot cross a COMP boundary and TOPs have no by-name reference parameter the way Select CHOP does for CHOPs. Deposits a tiny (0.0015-coefficient) seed-positioned mark per lexicon word every frame into feedback_sediment (bounded feedback loop, built bypassed first, reset=0 only after verifying passthrough) via level_sediment_decay (brightness1=Sedimentdecay, default 0.995, strictly <1) + comp_sediment_add. The deposit coefficient must stay tiny relative to (1-decay): the loop's steady-state value is deposit/(1-decay), and since every persistent word re-deposits every frame, too high a ratio saturates to solid white within seconds. Composited as a background substrate (over_sediment, render1 painted OVER the ink, render1's own background alpha=0/transparent so the ink shows through the void) before the mood wash, so recurring words fade in as a slow-building texture rather than a foreground flash. sediment_ctrl hosts Sedimentdecay/Sedimentamount/Sedimentreset (pulse, relayed to feedback_sediment's resetpulse via sediment_reset_relay, a Parameter Execute DAT, since pulse parameters can't be bound by expression).

          Lesson: Pixel Format left at "Use Input" on a chain rooted in a single-channel CHOP-to-TOP (registry/chopto_lexicon is genuinely mono, built with dataformat=r for texelFetch(...).r lookups) silently carries that mono-ness through every "useinput" node downstream - including the final composite (over_sediment), which then collapses the WHOLE FRAME's hue, not just the ink, since compositing duplicates R into G/B. All six sediment-chain TOPs (glsl_sediment_deposit, comp_sediment_add, feedback_sediment, level_sediment_decay, level_sediment_out, over_sediment) are set explicitly to "8-bit fixed (RGBA)" for this reason - never leave "useinput" downstream of a deliberately single-channel source.

          Affinity Wash: select_affinity bridges registry/scriptchop_affinity (the same cross-COMP CHOP-reference technique used throughout this project) -> lag_affinity (smoothing, Affinitylagtime) -> const_affinitycolor -> level_affinitywash (opacity = Affinityenable * Affinityamount * intensity), feeding moodwash_out as a third input (index 2, alongside over_sediment and level_moodwash) - moodwash_out is the shared ambient-wash hub for exactly this kind of addition. registry/GaiaRegistryExt tracks gaia/people/{name}/* the same dynamic way as objects/lexicon (alpha ramps on `present`, decays on absence); since Gaia provides no seed for people, each name's color comes from a locally-computed string hash, cached once per name. scriptchop_affinity's GetAffinityWash() aggregates everyone present into one (r,g,b,intensity): weight = presence-alpha * confidence, intensity = weighted-average affinity - a stranger barely tints the scene, a strong bond glows in proportion, multiple present people blend their identity colors together.

          Point-sprite additive blending (pointsprite_soul: blendop=add, srcblend=one, destblend=one) clips per-point color to white quickly once hundreds of points overlap. glsl_soulfx_compute's rim brightening is capped to 0.35+0.35*rim (peak channel stays ~0.665, safely under 1.0) so overlapping points still show internal gradient instead of flattening into a white shell; level_bloom (blacklevel 0.72, brightness2 1.2) and blur_bloom (size 12) are tuned tight so bloom only catches genuine highlights rather than smearing the remaining texture away.

          coolColor is (0.12, 0.95, 0.35) - green core, same peak channel magnitude as the tuning above so it still holds; warmColor (0.95, 0.28, 0.12, stress/smile accent) is unchanged, so high stress/smile still shifts the mix toward orange/red. Lesson: capturing intermediate TOPs one at a time in sequence (render1, then moodwash_out, then blur_bloom, then out_null) can return stale/inconsistently-cooked results relative to each other - always re-capture the actual final output fresh before judging whether a fix worked.

          Two webrenderTOPs (webrender1/webrender2) feed moodwash_out as additional additive inputs, compositing a sci-fi HUD/ring dashboard (level/archetype/vitals readout, glowing rings, particle starfield) over the soul core. soul_geo's scale is raised to 1.0 uniform (sx/sy/sz) so the core holds visual weight against that overlay instead of reading as a small dot in the middle.
        position: [-70, -2805]
        size: [5690, 3275]
        color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
      - name: annotate3
        mode: annotate
        title: Data (Canvas Schema)
        text: New gaia/canvas/* data extraction layer, parallel to the legacy 'data' COMP below. See internal annotation for details.
        position: [-800, -650]
        size: [587, 370]
        color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
      - name: annotate4
        mode: annotate
        title: Gaia Registry
        text: Dynamic per-key state (object classes, lexicon words) with seed + fade-in/out alpha. See internal annotation for details.
        position: [-900, -2425]
        size: [580, 370]
        color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
      - name: annotate5
        mode: annotate
        title: DMX Output (structure only, unarmed)
        text: |-
          select_lights_for_dmx (cross-boundary ref to data_canvas/null_lights_canvas) -> math_dmx_wash (gain=Lightscale, postoff=mood-wash contribution) -> merge_dmx -> limit_dmx (clamp 0-255) -> dmx_out1. Controlled from dmx_ctrl: Dmxenable (default OFF - safety switch, must be explicitly armed before any real hardware output), Washtodmxamount (mood wash fraction added to every fixture channel, additive so it reads even at power=0), Lightscale (raw-unit-to-255 multiplier, default 1.0 - all fixtures currently read 0 live, tune once real values are seen). dmx_patch table is a placeholder for the user to fill in fixture/universe/address once rig details are known. Protocol (Art-Net/sACN), universe, net/subnet left at defaults - structure only this pass.

          Virtual zone-color fixtures: script_zone_colors reads the 22 zones' final rendered Color attribute directly from zones_geo/glsl_zonelayout (the same on/off+brightness+motion+YOLO-presence-boost mix the visual actually shows per zone, not the raw Hue input state) as zone1_r..zone22_b (66 channels), scaled to 0-255 by math_zone_colors, merged with the existing house-mirroring channels in merge_dmx before the shared limit_dmx clamp - physical lights can be synced to the generative visual itself. Still gated by the same Dmxenable safety switch; these 66 channels have no routing table entries yet (structure only, unarmed - real fixture/universe/address assignment for a 22-fixture rig is the user's call).
        position: [3450, 625]
        size: [2087, 783]
        color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
      - name: annotate6
        mode: annotate
        title: Mocap Body Mirror
        text: |-
          Abstract "body mirror" driven by Gaia's gaia/mocap/ops-silvermini2/* feed (pose/hand/face landmarks, all three in use). mocap_bridge (MocapBridgeExt) is a DEFENSIVE adapter: the feed's channel addressing is unstable (pose/hand indices increment across tracking sessions instead of reusing fixed per-landmark slots; face is worse - mixed zero-padding widths like "01"/"010"/"0100"/"01000" sort out of numeric order alphabetically) - so identity is tracked by ACTIVITY (a channel's value changing between cooks, decaying like registry's alpha) rather than by literal channel name/index. A channel holding any real value stays visible at a STATIC_FLOOR alpha (0.3) even once it stops changing, since a manual/burst OSC test send has no continuous stream and would otherwise decay to invisible within ~1s.

          Bucketed active channels form up to 40 pose + 24+24 hand + 40 face points (128 total, grid_mocap sized 16x8). mocap_geo samples 4 CHOP-to-TOP textures (poseTex/handLTex/handRTex/faceTex) in a glslPOP compute shader (glsl_mocap), coloring each cluster with a distinct hue (pose 0.55 cyan, left hand 0.12 orange, right hand 0.92 pink, face 0.75 purple) mixed with mood color, fading via each point's activity-alpha.

          Lesson: pointsprite_mocap's Sizing Model is "Constant/Attenuate" with Attenuate Point Scale (attenpscale) raised to 0.6 (from a default of 0.0) and pointsize raised to 0.2 (from 0.025) - at attenpscale=0.0 the material completely ignores the shader's own PointScale attribute output and renders every point at the tiny constant size, which stayed invisible for a sparse, spread-out point cloud like this one (soul_geo's identical pointsize only looks visible because hundreds of densely-overlapping points accumulate brightness; a sparse body-tracing cloud has no such overlap). Attenuate Point Scale defaulting to 0.0 means a custom PointScale attribute from a compute shader has zero effect until raised - always verify a per-point size attribute is actually wired to something in the material, not just computed in the shader. A dedicated diagnostic render chain (mocap_preview_cam/mocap_preview_render/mocap_preview_out) stays in the network for isolating future render-visibility issues.

          Face construction: UpdateFace samples each of the 7 anatomical regions (lips/eye_left/eye_right/eyebrow_left/eyebrow_right/nose/oval, under gaia/mocap/ops-silvermini2/face/0/*) against a fixed per-region slot budget (_FACE_REGION_BUDGET: oval=10, lips=8, eye_left=6, eye_right=6, nose=6, eyebrow_left=2, eyebrow_right=2, summing to MAX_FACE_POINTS=40) so every region is always represented regardless of activity - pooling all regions globally and keeping the 40 most-active points let one busy region (e.g. lips while talking) crowd out the rest, producing a blob instead of a face. Within each region, points are sampled at evenly-spaced indices across that region's own contour (not top-K by activity), since MediaPipe contour indices are spatially ordered - this traces the region's actual outline shape instead of clustering on its busiest sub-area.
        position: [512, 577]
        size: [1328, 818]
        color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
      - name: annotate7
        mode: annotate
        title: Nursery Library (Canale 9)
        text: |-
          Pre-built, pre-tested components toggled by Bridge/gaia_nursery (MQTT gaia/nursery/activate|deactivate) -- see ARCHITECTURE.md §7 and GAIA_INTERFACE.md "Canale 9". Each component defaults to display=False/render=False (invisible, not cooking); the extension flips both flags and sets custom pars from the activation's params on activate, reverts on deactivate/TTL expiry. Whitelisted against nursery_components.json, never invented at runtime.

          person_sigil (trigger: person_recognized) -- wired into render1's Geometry list, appears in the main soul scene near recognition_geo. Custom pars: Hue, Shape (ring/spiral/cluster), Energy.
          dream_fragment (trigger: dream_new) -- wired into dream_render1's Geometry list (the separate dream-scene render, NOT the main render1), appears only when the dream crossfade is active. Custom pars: Hue, Shape (ring/spiral/cluster), Scale.

          Both share the same GLSL point-cluster technique (24 points, shape branches on an int uniform derived from the Shape menu) -- same pattern as recognition_geo/plantnotes_geo, kept deliberately small/cheap (confirmed negligible fps/GPU-mem impact via get_project_performance before/after).
        position: [1875, 600]
        size: [1289, 790]
        color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
      - name: annotate8
        mode: annotate
        title: Plant Note Sparks (outer particle ring)
        text: |-
          16-slot ring buffer (GaiaRegistryExt._plantSlots, independent of the ambient plant_out wash's single-per-room aggregate) - each plant_note spawns one fading spark, packed via script_plantnotes_tex (80 chans, attribute-major: 16 r,16 g,16 b,16 bright,16 roomNorm) -> chopto_plantnotes (1x80 tex, rowscropped) -> glsl_plantnotes texelFetch, same pattern as zones_geo's zoneTex. Positioned in a ring (radius ~2.15-2.4, just outside the zone light ring at 2.0) with per-slot hash jitter on angle/radius/height so simultaneous notes in one room don't stack.

          Lessons from building this chain (all three silent - no errors, just wrong/no visual): (1) create_op leaves a new POP chain's Display/Render flags OFF by default (unlike TD's UI, which auto-activates the last-created op) - a geometryCOMP renders whichever child has the Render flag, so it must be set explicitly. (2) primitivePOP defaults to NOT converting the grid to point primitives - needs method=set, setprimtype=points, set=all, keep=True explicitly (same fix as dream_geo/inhabitants_geo), otherwise the underlying quad topology still renders as filled shapes. (3) An op whose only input is a static grid, with zero EXPRESSION-mode parameters, and whose live data arrives purely via a texture SAMPLER (not a wired input), cooks once and caches forever - TD has no reason to think it needs re-evaluation. Fixed by adding a uTime uniform (absTime.seconds, EXPRESSION mode, used for a faint per-point twinkle) purely to give it a reason to re-cook on demand; the real trigger is "has at least one EXPRESSION-mode par," not "references absTime specifically" (zones_geo/glsl_zonelayout already re-cooks correctly because it has EXPRESSION-mode vec pars, with no uTime at all).

          Camera note: radius >~2.5 at this COMP's depth (z=0, same as zones_geo) is outside the frustum (cam at z=6, fov=45, soul_geo at z=-2) - invisible off-frame if the ring is ever widened.
        position: [3900, -2100]
        size: [1581, 500]
        color: [0.45, 0.45, 0.45]
    - name: MoodNudge
      type: baseCOMP
      custom_pars:
        Mood Nudge:
        - name: Deltastress
          style: Float
          label: Delta (Stress)
          startSection: true
          default: 0.1
          min: -1.0
          clampMin: true
          clampMax: true
          normMin: -1.0
          help: Amount to add to Gaia's stress mood dimension (0-1 scale, clamped by Gaia) on the next SendStress pulse. Negative subtracts.
          value: 0
        - name: Sendstress
          style: Pulse
          label: Send Stress
          help: Sends /gaia/td/mood/stress with the current Delta (Stress) value as a one-shot delta added to Gaia's live mood state.
        - name: Deltacalm
          style: Float
          label: Delta (Calm)
          startSection: true
          default: 0.1
          min: -1.0
          clampMin: true
          clampMax: true
          normMin: -1.0
          help: Amount to add to Gaia's calm mood dimension (0-1 scale, clamped by Gaia) on the next SendCalm pulse. Negative subtracts.
          value: 0
        - name: Sendcalm
          style: Pulse
          label: Send Calm
          help: Sends /gaia/td/mood/calm with the current Delta (Calm) value as a one-shot delta added to Gaia's live mood state.
        - name: Deltasocial
